# N3 example: base-and-literals.
# Companion to base-and-literals.eye/.srl: a language-tagged name and a
# plain numeric age, matching an adult filter that requires both the
# English language tag and an age of at least 18. `log:langlit` (reverse
# mode) decomposes the tagged literal into its (value, language) pair so
# the tag can be checked explicitly.

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#>.
@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#>.
@prefix : <http://example/>.

:alice :name "Alice Smith"@en; :age 22.
:bob :name "Bob"@nl; :age 17.

{?person :name ?name. ?person :age ?age. ?pair log:langlit ?name. ?pair list:firstRest (?value ?rest). ?rest list:firstRest (?lang ?rest2). ?lang log:equalTo "en". ?age math:notLessThan 18} => {?person :adult true}.
